# Foundry and Prettier both normalise to LF, and Git on Windows checks out CRLF by default — so a
# `git checkout` of a source file was enough to make `forge fmt --check` report every line of it as
# changed, locally and only locally. Pin the endings for the files those two tools own.
*.sol text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# `web:static` refuses to publish whitepaper.pdf if the sha256 of whitepaper.html has moved since
# it was rendered. Windows checking the source out as CRLF while Linux CI checks it out as LF would
# make that digest disagree with itself across platforms, on a file neither side edited.
*.html text eol=lf

# And the render itself is bytes. Nothing should ever decide it looks like text.
*.pdf binary
